SDK patch 0312 (Max Payne 3 port), amendment 2: the cvar is read once (the per-call read cost 600 us a draw
again - 2 fps). The tonemap's draws reuse the composite's texture set, so the first sampler loop skips them: its
inputs are provably the composite's (fine), which leaves its vertex shader as the noise source with the stencil
test off (a masked match on the quad's VS, the same disease as the costume spikes).

--- a/src/x360/deko/dibujos.cpp
+++ b/src/x360/deko/dibujos.cpp
@@ -1603,13 +1603,13 @@
       }
       const uint32_t* fetch = r + kRegFetch + uint32_t(sampler.registro) * 6;
       // 0312, x360_traza_fetch_escalado: which pixel shader and slot reads which texture with which scale, before the
       // fetch cache hides it. The scene and the bloom chain mix exp_adjust -11 and -13 reads of one resolved address;
       // the draw that reads it four times brighter than the game meant is what whitens lit textures, and only the
       // shader's number tells the two apart.
-      if (REXCVAR_GET(x360_traza_fetch_escalado)) {
+      if ([] { static const bool traza_ = REXCVAR_GET(x360_traza_fetch_escalado); return traza_; }()) {
         // 0316: every distinct (PS, slot, base, fmt, signos) - the tonemap's guest sampler (its HHSampler, slot 13,
         // has exp_adjust 0 and no signs, so no filter may hide it). The map grows with the real texture set only.
         static std::unordered_map<uint64_t, uint32_t> vistas_dibujo_;
         const int32_t fexp = int32_t(fetch[3] << 13) >> 26;
         const uint32_t fsignos = (fetch[0] >> 2) & 0xFF;
         const uint64_t clave = (uint64_t(ps->numero & 0xFFF) << 48) | (uint64_t(sampler.registro) << 44) |
